My guess is that this is due to the Nethack mythos' roots in (A)D&D, 
where there was made an early division between Occidental and Oriental 
campaigns, when the latter was introduced (AD&D Oriental Adventures, 
1985). Everything non-Oriental was already bundled together in the 
vanilla flavor. Oriental Adventures had its own campaign setting ,Kara-
Tur, like Greyhawk, Forgotten Realms etc of the standard version.

Not a reason, just a possible explanation.

